WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.249 --> 00:00:01.686
- [Woman] You know, you 
gentlemen are up there,

00:00:01.686 --> 00:00:05.308
do you think women can 
be the same as you guys

00:00:05.308 --> 00:00:07.492
sitting up there, saying 
things the same way

00:00:07.492 --> 00:00:09.853
and be accepted in the same way?

00:00:09.853 --> 00:00:14.699
- No. And I think that sucks but
I've thought about this a lot.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:18.306
I've thought about 
this a crap load.

00:00:18.306 --> 00:00:20.133
I invested in Birchbox.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.764
I wrote the first check
into that company

00:00:21.764 --> 00:00:26.494
and I sat in the pitch in 
Starbucks and said

00:00:26.494 --> 00:00:28.726
yes in 12 minutes.

00:00:28.726 --> 00:00:32.307
And they got super pumped
and emotional in a good way.

00:00:32.307 --> 00:00:34.628
Not in a cliché bullshit 
like women way

00:00:34.628 --> 00:00:35.632
just like pumped.

00:00:35.632 --> 00:00:37.602
And I asked them I was like

00:00:37.602 --> 00:00:40.333
I couldn't put my finger on it

00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:42.526
and they're like, "We've gotten
60 no's in a row,

00:00:42.526 --> 00:00:43.843
"You're our first yes."

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.827
And I was cool and I didn't 
really think much of it.

00:00:45.827 --> 00:00:48.177
It was the nicest day,
early in the spring

00:00:48.177 --> 00:00:50.381
it was the nicest day of 
the year four years ago.

00:00:50.381 --> 00:00:51.965
The first nice day, you know 
that awesome day that

00:00:51.965 --> 00:00:54.172
we love so much in New York.

00:00:54.172 --> 00:00:55.959
So I was like I'm gonna
walk home 'cause

00:00:55.959 --> 00:00:57.940
I was kinda in midtown,
I was going to Upper East Side.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.697
Somewhere around 
eight blocks in I was like,

00:00:59.697 --> 00:01:04.453
"Huh. I really wonder that 
idea was so obvious

00:01:04.453 --> 00:01:07.626
"I really wonder if those were 
two dudes would they

00:01:07.626 --> 00:01:10.539
"get 11 yes's instead of one?"

00:01:12.199 --> 00:01:14.431
You have to understand,
and this is not even close,

00:01:14.431 --> 00:01:16.443
my mom, my wife and

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:19.165
my first-born daughter 
are my life. Right?

00:01:19.165 --> 00:01:20.826
I love my bro and 
my dad and all this

00:01:20.826 --> 00:01:22.337
but that is my world

00:01:22.337 --> 00:01:26.456
and I, if God, you know
I actually don't care

00:01:26.456 --> 00:01:28.932
if my daughter, god willing,
would want to be a

00:01:28.932 --> 00:01:30.035
big time entrepreneur and CEO

00:01:30.035 --> 00:01:32.572
I would want her to 
dominate the world

00:01:32.572 --> 00:01:34.654
and I think that people 
want to look at the world

00:01:34.654 --> 00:01:37.746
through rosy glasses
or very cynical glasses.

00:01:37.746 --> 00:01:40.610
And I think the answer is
always in-between.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:42.942
There's a million 
women entrepreneurs

00:01:42.942 --> 00:01:45.234
or storytellers that 
are killing it. Right?

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:48.058
We have to recognize that the 
way the market consumes

00:01:48.058 --> 00:01:50.659
people is different based 
on if they're a woman,

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:52.070
if they're African-American,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.647
if they're Muslim-American,
just a million.

00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:57.339
How about pretty?

00:01:57.339 --> 00:01:59.160
How about just being pretty?

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.370
Versus not being 
as pretty. Right?

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:05.072
There's a million variables in 
play and I think it's insane.

00:02:05.072 --> 00:02:07.612
I come from the Soviet Union.

00:02:07.612 --> 00:02:09.741
Right? Where everything being 
the same is the game.

00:02:09.741 --> 00:02:11.810
It's just not real. Right?

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.300
By the way, it doesn't 
mean that it's worse,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.452
it doesn't mean 
that it's worse at all.

00:02:16.452 --> 00:02:18.114
It just means that it's different.

00:02:18.114 --> 00:02:19.029
So is it the same?

00:02:19.029 --> 00:02:19.970
No, it's not the same.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.809
'Cause everybody's gonna 
consume it differently.

00:02:21.809 --> 00:02:25.006
It's also not the same for each,

00:02:25.006 --> 00:02:26.385
you're an African-American woman

00:02:26.385 --> 00:02:27.856
the way that you're consuming me

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:30.338
is different than those 
two Russian guys over there

00:02:30.338 --> 00:02:33.470
who have a connection point 
with me that's different.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:37.564
I think this whole notion 
of is it the same,

00:02:37.564 --> 00:02:38.502
of course it's not.

00:02:38.502 --> 00:02:39.728
It's a silly question.

00:02:39.728 --> 00:02:41.794
I think what's more important is

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.494
I'm a big believer of 
betting on your strengths

00:02:44.494 --> 00:02:45.814
and I spoke to it earlier.

00:02:45.814 --> 00:02:48.048
Again, I won the 
lotto completely.

00:02:48.048 --> 00:02:50.629
White male in America
and born in the Soviet Union.

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:52.045
I won triple big.

00:02:52.045 --> 00:02:56.930
I think that we have to 
understand how things work.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:59.414
But I'll tell you that,
how about this

00:02:59.414 --> 00:03:02.273
Casey and I did a video 
together the other day

00:03:02.273 --> 00:03:05.375
Casey's fanbase hated me

00:03:05.375 --> 00:03:08.698
as a net score because I talked 
over him during the show.

00:03:08.698 --> 00:03:10.654
'Cause I get hyper 
and this and that.

00:03:10.654 --> 00:03:12.789
And I went into my own channel
and had to apologize

00:03:12.789 --> 00:03:15.935
to like 500 people that came
over from Casey's world

00:03:15.935 --> 00:03:18.690
and said, "GaryVee, fuck you.
You suck shit."

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.220
(laughter)

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.984
Need to spend less time of
what we can't be and

00:03:22.984 --> 00:03:25.873
we need to spend more 
time on what we can be.

